{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And you shall distinguish between the clean beast and the unclean.</b> No need to say between a cow and a donkey — they are already distinguished and recognizable. Rather, between clean for you and unclean for you — between one whose greater part of the sign was slaughtered and one whose half was slaughtered. And how much is between the greater part and the half? A hair's breadth (Sifra)." "<b>which I have distinguished for you as unclean.</b> To forbid."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:27.600095239Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}